#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:5
#: b591068fa2d24016a3fb25151560e067
msgid "Mission Planner Simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:7
#: ccfa950357b3475fa4546d39efd3bb89
msgid "The Simulation tab provides a SITL (Software in the Loop) simulation capability. Many typical frame types for each Vehicle type have been created. This allows you to see the expected behavior for vehicles in missions, or with a joystick attached, actually be able to fly/drive the vehicle simulation as if with RC. This allows you to see potential effects of parameter changes on vehicle behavior or explore mission generation, without risking your vehicle first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:9
#: 5bb62a7f25af4246adad2bedfe1fcdac
msgid "Demonstration Video"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:15
#: 2778d47cc757441bb40baeb887195178
msgid "Setup and Use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:17
#: 9341904ebd4d4bfc8208e7e6695c26b8
msgid "The Simulation uses the same SITL models as those used in the Linux ``sim_vehicle.py`` script (see :ref:`dev:sitl-simulator-software-in-the-loop`, and uses the current master development branch of the code for firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:19
#: 4af82c7a5b15443a8aa0b24271c7a445
msgid "Open Mission Planner's **Simulation** tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:20
#: b505d3c8dd4f492da609aa23582b0ce4
msgid "Choose your vehicle type and frame (the \"Model\" drop down box). First select the \"Model\" frame type, then click the vehicle it corresponds to. If no \"Model\" (frame) is selected, then a normal plane will be used no matter what vehicle is clicked. If a frame is selected and a vehicle clicked that does NOT correspond to it, undefined results may occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:21
#: fbed9a1119454f349e3cded8fa61a893
msgid "Default parameters for that vehicle/frame will be loaded and the simulation started. Mission Planner can be used to control the vehicle, setup missions, alter parameters, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:22
#: a372e60cae264ad1a8fc8c32f7135fab
msgid "In addition to the normal vehicle parameters, you can also now see and change the \"SIM_x\" (simulation) parameters via the CONFIG/Full Parameter Tree page. See :ref:`dev:sitl-parameters` for a list of these."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:25
#: 24d9dfe08f374de58a6d611e23438878
msgid "Extra Command Line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:27
#: e8b6ccda1e1a4b71b0d8e35d4253f770
msgid "The ``Extra command line`` box on the SIMULATION tab, you can start the SITL with various options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:29
#: 5150e349b38847b1afe7072d04e6bb82
msgid "Home Location : start simulation at any given location using the command ``--home={location}`` where location can be either gps coordinates,altitude ASL and vehicle initial heading, or a named location in the `Autotest locations file <https://github.com/ardupilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/autotest/locations.txt>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:36
#: a11a243b63784215b7030a9c6028dfb5
msgid "Different Default Parameter File: allows using a different default parameter file. If used in conjunctions with the ``Wipe`` checkbox (which wipes any previously changed parameters while running simulations on the chosen vehicle), these parameters will be loaded at simulation start. This avoids having to load and store any parameters desired to be changed for the simulation from the normal defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:42
#: eaf08bed37bc4c3a9d66fcb4ac20b7da
msgid "Attach a physical device to a SERIALx port in the sim: You can attach actual devices (GPS, RC, Rangefinder,etc.) to a Windows serial COM port and have it attached to a SERIALx port in the simulation for testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:49
#: 07b77e108b58485fbe31de2ce516e6f3
msgid "Although not shown in the above video, current version of Mission Plannner will ask if you want to simulate using the Development(master aka \"latest\") or Stable version of the vehicle firmware when you click the vehicle to download the model and parameters and begin the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:52
#: 570c83009bb34545bb5acd43ec464a50
msgid "Simulating Custom Code Branches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-simulation.rst:54
#: 8566c21ed5f14cf187376e71963bac51
msgid "In addition, if you are code developer, you can run SITL using your custom code branch using Mission Planner, either with or without, the physics and visualizations of RealFlight. See the :ref:`Using Your Code Branch with Mission Planner SITL and RealFlightM<mp-sitl-custom-code>` section of :ref:`dev:sitl-with-realflight`"
msgstr ""
